# TEMPLATE — copy to cloudflare-api-token.yaml and fill in the real token,
# same convention as secret.yaml.example. The un-suffixed filename is
# git-ignored so it can never be committed with a live credential.
#
#   cp k8s/cloudflare-api-token.yaml.example k8s/cloudflare-api-token.yaml
#   # edit in the real token, then:
#   kubectl apply -f k8s/cloudflare-api-token.yaml
#
# NAMESPACE IS `cert-manager`, NOT `skillstreak`, and this is the single
# most common way a DNS01 setup fails. ClusterIssuers are cluster-scoped,
# so they resolve secret references in cert-manager's
# `--cluster-resource-namespace` (which on this cluster resolves to
# `cert-manager`). A token applied into `skillstreak` alongside everything
# else in this directory is simply never read, and the resulting Challenge
# error does not say "wrong namespace" — it looks like a bad token.
#
# CREATING THE TOKEN (Cloudflare dashboard -> My Profile -> API Tokens ->
# Create Token -> "Edit zone DNS" template):
#
#   Permissions:  Zone / DNS   / Edit
#                 Zone / Zone  / Read
#   Zone resources: Include / Specific zone / skillstreak.xyz
#
# Use an API *token*, never the Global API Key. The global key can do
# anything to any zone on the account, cannot be scoped, and cannot be
# revoked without breaking every other thing using it. This token can
# write DNS records in one zone and nothing else — that is the entire
# blast radius if the cluster is ever compromised.
#
# Zone:Read is required in addition to DNS:Edit: cert-manager looks up the
# zone ID for the name it is solving before it can write the TXT record.
# With DNS:Edit alone, issuance fails at zone lookup.
#
# ROTATION: create the replacement token in Cloudflare first, re-apply
# this Secret, then delete the old token. cert-manager picks the new value
# up on its next solve — there is nothing to restart, and no certificate
# is at risk mid-rotation because existing certs are already issued.
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: cloudflare-api-token
  namespace: cert-manager
type: Opaque
stringData:
  api-token: CHANGE_ME
